[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: "the parser reads dates month first". The
reports in it, <ProblemCount ticket={4471} /> of them, are about **three** different problems. Subject lines could not tell them apart (every one says "wrong day"), so dedupe by
subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put them in one ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 was closed on 5 October after one fix. Two of the three problems below are still open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} tickets={TICKETS} />

Counts are unique reports: the ticket export repeats some reports across pages, so it has more
rows than reports. A report belongs to a problem by its tenant and the way it came in, not by
the tag intake gave it.

## The three problems

### `parser`: month read first · <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports · <a href={TICKETS.parser}>ticket</a>

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day first, so
any date with a day up to 12 comes out swapped: "booked 7 April, invite for 4 July".
Engineering shipped `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Check its scope before you tell a
tenant it is fixed: our day-first tenants include en-GB and en-IE, and "eu locales" may not
cover en-GB.

### `hint`: booking-v3 form hint · <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports · <a href={TICKETS.hint}>ticket</a>

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and reads the date day first.
People type what the hint says. Only reports that came through the form of a booking-v3 tenant
belong here: <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" what="tenants" /> tenants. The parser fix
does not touch it. Engineering answered "won't fix: booking-v3 form retired", but the tenant
directory still lists these tenants on booking-v3. Until they move, it keeps happening.

### `shift`: one day off · <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="shift" /> reports · <a href={TICKETS.shift}>ticket</a>

Not a swap at all. The date moved by one day, or two people in different places got different
days for one meeting. That points at time zones, not date order. The desk already read these as
a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), but the old table filed them under `parser` by tenant. No
fix covers them.

## For the desk

- A new date report: check the tenant's form and the dates in the body before you merge.
  Swapped day and month on booking-v3's form is `hint`; swapped elsewhere is `parser`; one day
  off is `shift`.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the browser: it is wrong on
  <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" what="mistagged" /> <code>parser</code>,
  <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" what="mistagged" /> <code>hint</code> and
  <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="shift" what="mistagged" /> <code>shift</code> reports here.
- Same subject does not mean same problem. Read the body when the subject is generic.

